WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:15.869 --> 00:00:16.900
Come on in.

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:18.829
Welcome to The Theory Place.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:26.760
Hello internet!

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.040
Welcome to Film Theory!

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:32.540
The greatest forking show on the whole Dame-Helen-Mirren internet!

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:35.820
I know we're all children of digital video and streaming services at this point,

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:36.820
but sometimes,

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:42.500
sometimes traditional TV surprises us and produces something that is really special.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:47.900
Enter "The Good Place", which is probably better titled "The Great Place" 'cause it's an awesome show.

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:49.640
And I'm not just saying that because Kristen Bell

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:52.660
has been my celebrity crush since her appearance in the musical "Reefer Madness".

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:56.629
No, I'm saying it because "The Good Place" is one of the best most heartfelt,

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:59.860
well written and original sitcoms I've ever seen.

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:02.620
I can't even imagine what the pitch meeting for this one must have looked like,

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:03.670
but I'm gonna try...

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:06.400
*dream sequence- dream sequence- dream sequence*

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:08.640
"So you have a sitcom for me?"

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:13.940
"Yes, sir, I do. It's about people in the afterlife, delving deeply into moral philosophy."

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.220
"Sorry, did you say moral philosophy?"

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:20.680
"Yeah, you know like Aristotelian virtue ethics and Kantian Deontology."

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.720
"And you expect people to watch this?"

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:25.400
"Yeah, yeah, yeah. I mean who doesn't love moral philosophy?"

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:26.640
"Pretty much everyone!"

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:30.979
Wow, that was a shockingly vivid dream sequence.

00:01:30.979 --> 00:01:33.220
But somehow, that formula's been amazing.

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:36.460
managing to both teach its audience about deep philosophical theory,

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:38.980
while also making unique jokes on the subject.

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:42.060
"It's like, who died and left Aristotle in charge of ethics?"

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:43.740
"Plato!"

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:49.360
And a big part of the show's appeal has been its ability to shock, surprise, and fake out not just its characters,

00:01:49.369 --> 00:01:51.460
but also the audience at home watching.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:54.700
Nothing demonstrates this better than the first season's arc.

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:57.620
Season 1 starts telling us the story of Eleanor Shellstrop,

00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:00.229
a recently deceased, who finds herself in paradise.

00:02:00.229 --> 00:02:02.140
We're told by one of heaven's architects, Michael,

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:04.600
that she is in "the Good Place".

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:08.880
"In the afterlife, there's a good place and there's a bad place."

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:10.460
"You're in the good place."

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:11.940
Except there's one problem here.

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:15.320
Something's wrong, Eleanor wasn't a good person on Earth.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:19.206
"You need me to lie to old people and scare them into buying fake medicine, I get it man."

00:02:19.206 --> 00:02:22.360
She was, as she describes herself "an Arizona trashbag"

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:23.420
"Those aren't my memories."

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:25.640
"I wasn't a lawyer, I never went to the Ukraine."

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:26.940
"I hate clowns."

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:28.700
"I'm not supposed to be here."

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:30.680
But that isn't the twist of the season,

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:32.800
and neither is the reveal three episodes later,

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:34.560
that silent Buddhist monk Jian Yu

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:38.140
is actually a failed DJ from Jacksonville, Florida named Jason Mendoza.

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:39.560
"Is your real name Jian Yu?"

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:40.980
"It's Jason Mendoza."

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:44.300
"And by the way, everyone here thinks I'm Taiwanese. I'm Filipino."

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:45.349
"Heaven is so racist."

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:48.100
No, the big twist comes in the season finale,

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.760
when Eleanor figures it all out,

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:53.780
that this is not the Good Place, but rather the Bad Place.

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:58.700
"Holy mother-forking shirt balls."

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:03.700
"Just now as we were all fighting, I thought to myself: Man, this is torture."

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:04.860
"and then it hit me."

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:06.230
"This is the Bad Place!"

00:03:06.230 --> 00:03:13.840
"Oh, it looks like paradise, but it's actually a filthy dumpster full of our worst anxieties."

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:15.840
*laughs*

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:19.520
"Oh man, I can't believe you figured it out!"

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:22.940
We learned that Michael, our heavenly guide from the very first scene of the show,

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:25.240
is actually a bad place architect.

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:29.800
A literal demon in disguise, who wanted to create a unique torture chamber for humans,

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:32.780
rather than inflicting just physical pain all the time,

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:35.900
Michael devised a system that used psychological torture,

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:39.880
by placing four people in a fake Good Place and having them torture each other.

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:45.240
It's a huge mind blow that, when you go back and re- watch the season again in this context,

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:48.080
was hidden in front of your eyes from the very start.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:49.760
The lack of steps in Eleanor's house,

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:52.360
the creepy clown pictures that populate everywhere,

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:55.600
the fact that the only restaurants in town serve frozen yogurt,

00:03:55.609 --> 00:03:59.440
"What's a food that people think they enjoy, but that's also kind of a bummer?"

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:00.280
"Frozen yogurt."

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:04.880
And that's only one of several massive reveals that occur throughout the series.

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:10.520
It's a smart show, one that's a bit bigger brained, and it holds its cards close to its chest.

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:15.530
So close, in fact, I believe that there's one final reveal the show has left for us to discover.

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:17.920
True, the last episode of "The Good Place" just aired,

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:21.948
and yes, I wept ugly, ugly tears at Chidi's "Waves on the sand" speech,

00:04:21.948 --> 00:04:24.620
but through it all, I also remained skeptical.

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:29.029
Because if you look at the series as a whole, even up to it's very final episode,

00:04:29.029 --> 00:04:33.500
It's pretty clear that this show wasn't just the tale of four humans and a heck demon

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.760
learning moral philosophy and becoming better people.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:44.200
No! This show from chapter 1, all the way through chapter 53 has always been the story of one man's eternal torture.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:45.140
That's right!

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:49.240
While we were all watching Eleanor and her friends trying to get out of The Bad Place and save the afterlife,

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:52.680
what we were actually witnessing was Michael's torture.

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:54.980
This isn't Eleanor's afterlife, it's his.

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:57.239
This is Michael's eternal suffering.

00:04:57.240 --> 00:05:00.560
He's the real one in The Bad Place in this series.

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:03.700
And if I'm wrong, well, then that's just a big ol' pile of bull-shirt.

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:05.960
If you follow Michael's journey throughout the series,

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:09.600
you clearly see that it's a repeated string of failure and insecurity.

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:13.340
Even before the humans come into his neighborhood, he's already freaking out.

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:15.940
"That was the last... pudding shop..."

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:18.640
"No, no, no, wait, wait, wait! This is all wrong!

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:19.920
"Pudding won't work!"

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:23.480
"Whoa, I'm way out on a limb here- and I'm all alone."

00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:25.500
And it doesn't help that he can't afford to fail.

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:29.129
Sure, he got his boss Shawn to agree to this revolutionary torture experiment,

00:05:29.129 --> 00:05:31.260
but if the plan fails, he'll be retired.

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:35.480
And not like cool retirement, like taking Greyhound buses to Vegas to sit at slot machines all day,

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:38.820
No, this is demon retirement, which is slightly worse.

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:40.840
"My soul will be disintegrated,"

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:45.180
"my essence will be scooped out of my body with a flaming ladle"

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:50.620
"and poured over hot diamonds, and then what's left of my body will be endlessly beaten with a titanium rod."

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:51.760
"Like a pinata."

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:58.050
"Yes, except you have the string around my waist, but instead it will definitely be around my genitals."

00:05:58.050 --> 00:06:01.380
But not only is he having to deal with the stress of being all alone

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:04.600
with a literal burning ladle waiting for him, his plan fails.

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:08.069
Eleanor figures out that they're in The Bad Place ruining all of Michael's work.

00:06:08.069 --> 00:06:12.540
He had promised his boss that they'd be able to torture people like this for a thousand years.

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:17.320
Instead, he barely gets six months out of it, forcing him to beg for just one more try.

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:18.960
Shawn grants him one more attempt.

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:20.250
"Good luck with attempt number two."

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:21.880
"There will be no attempt number three."

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:26.969
And yet over and over, time and again Eleanor figures out that they're in The Bad Place.

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:31.600
Michael ends up rebooting his neighborhood over 800 more times,

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:33.200
trying to figure out the way to get it right.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:34.020
And he can't.

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:37.700
It is a literal torture for him as he learns that no matter what he does,

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:40.480
he isn't good enough to make his plan work.

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:43.760
His dream of revolutionizing The Bad Place is shattered.

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:48.560
his life is on the line, which then results in him having to beg the humans for help.

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:51.940
"Suffice to say I tried more than two times."

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:54.720
"If he finds out we're all in hot water. Literally."

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:58.940
"We will be the main ingredient in a chowder of pain."

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:04.180
He devises a plan where the humans pretend like they don't know what's going on to fool all the rest of The Bad Place,

00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:09.140
the only catch is that now he, Michael, has to take moral philosophy classes with the rest of them,

00:07:09.140 --> 00:07:12.680
and again, this is another form of torture for Michael.

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:16.080
not just because Kantian Ethics is so dry and boring,

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:20.140
and why did I spend a senior year college semester learning it when I didn't even need the credit.

00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:21.520
What was I thinking?

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:27.880
Erm, but learning human morality literally sends Michael into a spiraling existential crisis.

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:30.260
In short, by the first couple episodes of Season 2,

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:33.740
he went from a confident nearly immortal being living his life,

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:36.300
to an insecure mask contemplating his own demise.

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:38.760
Definitely not a good trajectory for the guy.

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:40.940
As team cockroach works to fool the demons,

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:42.680
Michael becomes attached to the humans,

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:46.200
which only makes it worse because he can't figure out a way to help them.

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:47.410
He's made friends

00:07:47.410 --> 00:07:49.180
he's growing emotional attachments to them,

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:53.769
and yet he's been lying to their faces about his ability to help them the entire time.

00:07:53.770 --> 00:07:54.880
It's torture.

00:07:54.880 --> 00:07:58.660
Yet again putting Michael at an even lower low than he was before.

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:04.600
"So not only did I fail at getting us into The Good Place, I also learned the error of my ways."

00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:07.800
"Real rock-bottom for a demon. I'll tell you."

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:09.960
And it just doesn't get any better for him.

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:16.880
For the final two seasons, there is literally noone in the universe willing and able to help him save himself and the humans.

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:19.820
When he learns that there's a problem with the afterlife's point system,

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:22.320
he petitions the accountants to help, they don't.

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:26.619
"Neil, be logical. The bad place has hacked your system!"

00:08:26.620 --> 00:08:29.170
"No it hasn't. How dare you!"

00:08:29.170 --> 00:08:32.650
When he calls on the Leadership Committee of The Good Place trying to lay out the problems with the system,

00:08:32.810 --> 00:08:34.760
they again are useless.

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:37.120
"Michael, we have rules, procedures."

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:39.900
"We're the good guys, we can't just do stuff!"

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:46.000
Even after Michael overwhelmingly proves that humanity has the capacity for self-improvement in the final season,

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:50.420
the intergalactic judges verdict is that humanity needs to be wiped clean.

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:54.159
"You came to me and said the point system was flawed, and I've come to the conclusion..."

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:57.290
"...That you're right."

00:08:57.290 --> 00:08:59.290
*cheers*

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:04.380
"Now, in terms of how we handle this moving forward, obviously, Earth is cancelled."

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:07.280
"All humans on Earth in and the afterlife will be extinguished."

00:09:07.379 --> 00:09:11.200
"And we will start the entire human race over from scratch."

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:13.180
Then even when he finds a solution to that problem,

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:16.360
someone better than him takes over and removes his sense of purpose.

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:19.379
"I have to roll a rock up a hill!"

00:09:19.380 --> 00:09:27.840
"Over and over, and then Vicky comes along with this rock lifter thing and just lifts up to the top of the hill."

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:29.960
"Who am I if the rock is gone?"

00:09:30.029 --> 00:09:33.680
Not even The Good Place is a safe place for Michael.

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:36.960
Michael eventually earns his way to heaven and is greeted by the good place leadership committee,

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:40.480
only to then immediately be swindled by them.

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:42.979
"Now you are officially in charge of The Good Place."

00:09:43.259 --> 00:09:44.880
"I'm sorry, in charge?"

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:49.459
"Yep, you're the boss now, that was all legally binding and we all quit, effective immediately."

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:53.460
"So it's all your problem now, don't try to find us, no take-backs, okay, bye-bye!"

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:56.440
Yet again Michael is faced with a seemingly impossible problem.

00:09:56.440 --> 00:09:59.380
How do you make eternity palatable for the people living there?

00:09:59.380 --> 00:10:03.199
Paradise isn't Paradise if it goes on forever, it just becomes mind-numbing and boring,

00:10:03.199 --> 00:10:05.440
It's a problem that The Good Place committee couldn't solve,

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:09.258
and so they just dumped their problems onto, you guessed it, Michael.

00:10:09.259 --> 00:10:12.440
I think this quote from his former boss Shawn sums things up best.

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:16.820
"You won, and you still somehow failed. Classic."

00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:20.480
The long and short of it is that time and time and time again throughout the series,

00:10:20.480 --> 00:10:24.230
Michael is put into impossible situations and is given zero help.

00:10:24.230 --> 00:10:26.080
He's given his dream job opportunity,

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:29.599
only to see his ideas fail hundreds of times, with his life on the line,

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:32.760
He forms emotional bonds with people on the premise of lies.

00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:36.379
He becomes aware of, and immediately scared by his own ability to die.

00:10:36.379 --> 00:10:39.980
He's trapped in a perpetual cycle of ineffectual bureaucracy.

00:10:39.980 --> 00:10:43.489
Even the arbiters of heaven themselves dump their problems onto him.

00:10:43.490 --> 00:10:48.799
It sucks for Michael constantly in the show, and it never once lets up.

00:10:48.809 --> 00:10:53.999
That is the type of torture that Michael was trying to create for his human subjects, but in reality,

00:10:53.999 --> 00:10:57.300
it's just him undergoing it the entire series.

00:10:57.300 --> 00:11:01.940
Add to that all the small little inconveniences, with demons being uncomfortable in their human skin suits,

00:11:01.940 --> 00:11:03.920
"The suits are really itchy for us."

00:11:03.920 --> 00:11:06.540
"Every part of my body's either too dry or too wet."

00:11:06.550 --> 00:11:10.060
"I got to say it took me a long time to get used to the hanging bits."

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:10.840
"Gross."

00:11:10.840 --> 00:11:14.420
"Get your mind out of the gutter, Eleanor, I was talking about my testicles."

00:11:14.420 --> 00:11:17.460
And it's clear that Michael is miserable the entire time,

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:20.590
but what's really suspicious is that Michael is never retired.

00:11:20.590 --> 00:11:25.100
You see he is captured, there are multiple opportunities for him to be dispatched with,

00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:26.700
and yet he never is.

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:29.720
In fact, the whole retirement thing is just a bunch of smoke and mirrors.

00:11:29.720 --> 00:11:30.820
"Retirement is a spectacle."

00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:33.140
"Everyone would see the flaming ladles good on your throat."

00:11:33.140 --> 00:11:34.300
"Then they'd ask me what you did."

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:35.740
"I don't need that kind of scrutiny right now."

00:11:35.740 --> 00:11:38.140
It's an odd wrinkle of the show that gets explained away.

00:11:38.140 --> 00:11:42.160
If Michael is actually the person in the bad place getting tortured.

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:44.170
You see, he finds himself in a catch-22.

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:46.820
They can't kill him, because he's being tortured.

00:11:46.820 --> 00:11:48.489
It would be the end of his eternal torment,

00:11:48.490 --> 00:11:52.160
so instead they scare him with the prospect of retirement until he gets too close to it,

00:11:52.160 --> 00:11:54.720
at which point they need to make up some excuse to delay it,

00:11:54.720 --> 00:11:57.100
and get him back on track with the ceaseless misery.

00:11:57.100 --> 00:12:00.000
And wouldn't you know it, it's the exact same loophole

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:04.120
that helps Eleanor figure out that the humans are trapped in the bad place

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:07.720
"They're never gonna call a train to take us to The Bad Place."

00:12:07.720 --> 00:12:10.340
"They can't, because we're already here."

00:12:10.360 --> 00:12:12.200
"This is the bad place."

00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:16.080
And here's my favorite part: like all the best twists in the series,

00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:18.580
the show outright tells us what it's doing.

00:12:18.580 --> 00:12:23.200
In Season 3 Episode 7, Eleanor outright predicts this:

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:28.287
"Maybe there's a mega demon who built a torture chamber for demons, and this whole thing is just him torturing you."

00:12:28.287 --> 00:12:30.040
When I first saw this episode, I thought,

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:33.220
"Aw dip! They wouldn't actually call attention to a major plot twist like this."

00:12:33.320 --> 00:12:34.760
Except, they totally would.

00:12:34.760 --> 00:12:39.800
Way back before anybody knew what was going on, in the very first episode of the show,

00:12:39.800 --> 00:12:42.680
Eleanor practically guesses what's really going on.

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:47.040
"My parents were divorced when I was a kid. They're probably in the bad place."

00:12:47.050 --> 00:12:50.020
"Maybe they're being used to torture each other. It would work."

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:52.580
And they don't just pull that trick once, they do it twice.

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:54.980
"I think we might be in an alien zoo or on a prank show."

00:12:54.980 --> 00:12:56.160
"No, Jian you are dead."

00:12:56.170 --> 00:12:59.740
They even call back to it after the big reveal to show off how clever they were.

00:12:59.740 --> 00:13:03.580
"Oh, dude I told you that first night that we were in a prank show."

00:13:03.580 --> 00:13:06.500
"Oh, yeah, you did! Great job, man!"

00:13:06.500 --> 00:13:08.680
So it seems like The Good Place (the show)

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:11.410
was in the habit of giving up the ghost before we know what's going on.

00:13:11.410 --> 00:13:15.340
But this time, we have enough information from which to draw our own conclusions.

00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:17.020
Fool me once, shame on you.

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:21.320
Fool me twice, well, I'll probably just wind up doing another episode on the topic.

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:25.780
Now admittedly, the final episode of the show is a bit hard to explain away under this theory.

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:28.780
Michael gets his ultimate wish and gets to live out his life as a human,

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:32.200
and our hearts are warmed as he learns the guitar without the help of Janet,

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:34.620
and finally gets to say to someone that iconic phrase,

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:35.549
"Take it sleazy."

00:13:35.549 --> 00:13:39.200
But put aside the sappy music for a second, and let's be clear here,

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:41.100
Michael is a human now,

00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:45.500
and as this show has made patently clear, being on Earth kind of sucks.

00:13:45.500 --> 00:13:47.240
"That was rough!"

00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:50.480
"Sheesh! Earth is a mess!"

00:13:50.520 --> 00:13:53.560
And being a human is a lifetime full of sadness.

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:55.420
"You're learning what it's like to be human."

00:13:55.420 --> 00:13:59.380
"All humans are aware of death, so we're all a little bit sad, all the time."

00:13:59.380 --> 00:14:01.620
"Sounds like a crappy deal."

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:02.460
"Yeah, it is."

00:14:02.460 --> 00:14:04.980
Not only that, but he loses all of his friends.

00:14:04.980 --> 00:14:08.660
At the end of the show, he sees all of his friends leave and become space dust.

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:10.280
He's separated from Janet.

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:11.720
Sure he'll meet new friends now,

00:14:11.720 --> 00:14:15.329
but when he returns to the afterlife, all his new friends will eventually dust as well

00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:19.560
he'll perpetually see people he cares about leave and leave and leave,

00:14:19.560 --> 00:14:20.460
but he never can.

00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:22.720
It's only a matter of time before he breaks in.

00:14:22.720 --> 00:14:27.660
In short, Michael's existence is one of ceaseless torment, insecurity and constant disappointment.

00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:31.540
He's perpetually forced into positions where he's the only one who can solve a problem,

00:14:31.540 --> 00:14:34.540
and even when he does, someone steps in and does it better than him.

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:39.210
Even heaven itself tricks and abandons him to figure out an eternity of unsolved problems,

00:14:39.210 --> 00:14:41.879
which in and of itself is pretty darn suspicious, since you know,

00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:44.620
it's heaven, probably shouldn't be doing stuff like that there.

00:14:44.620 --> 00:14:48.960
Any way you slice it, it seems like Michael is the one in the Bad Place here,

00:14:48.960 --> 00:14:52.580
If The Bad Place is truly a place of ceaseless misery and torment.

00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:55.769
Well, that is Michael's experience throughout the course of this show.

00:14:55.770 --> 00:14:58.040
But it all wraps up happily ever after, right?

00:14:58.040 --> 00:14:59.549
He gets to be human, a creature,

00:14:59.550 --> 00:15:00.940
that is always uncomfortable,

00:15:00.940 --> 00:15:03.740
Always sad, and always one margarita mix away

00:15:03.740 --> 00:15:05.940
from getting run over by a train of shopping carts.

00:15:05.940 --> 00:15:08.140
The ending of the show is meant to be happy,

00:15:08.140 --> 00:15:11.640
but really it just shows that humanity is the pinnacle of torture.

00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:14.520
But hey! That's just a theory!

00:15:14.520 --> 00:15:16.720
A Film Theory!

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:17.740
Aaand...

00:15:17.740 --> 00:15:18.570
Forknuggets!

00:15:18.570 --> 00:15:23.640
I forgot to send a special thanks to Ryan from Screen Rant for his little pitch meeting cameo at the top of this episode.

00:15:23.640 --> 00:15:26.120
If you enjoyed that or this theory,

00:15:26.120 --> 00:15:29.380
then make sure to check out him and his series Pitch Meeting over on that channel,

00:15:29.380 --> 00:15:31.049
link is right on screen right now.

00:15:31.050 --> 00:15:35.900
They have over a hundred pitch meetings for you to binge and enjoy like I have multiple times.

00:15:35.900 --> 00:15:37.900
And hey, if you did like this episode, let me know.

00:15:37.900 --> 00:15:41.099
Honestly, I have another really good idea for another "Good Place" theory.

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:43.800
but wasn't sure if you guys would actually care about this show at all,

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:45.320
So let me know if that was fun for you.

00:15:45.320 --> 00:15:47.154
And with that, my friends, I'm off.

00:15:47.154 --> 00:15:48.149
Keep it sleazy guys!

00:15:48.149 --> 00:15:49.820
"I wanted to eat a Saltine."

00:15:49.820 --> 00:15:50.740
"Pretty dry."

00:15:50.740 --> 00:15:51.780
"And too salty."

00:15:51.780 --> 00:15:53.518
"Going out on a real low note here."

